WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:02.969
-Today, the president reeled off

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.704
a deranged tirade
at the White House,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.973
where he celebrated
his sham impeachment acquittal

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.674
with his Republican
co-conspirators.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.743
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.211
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.814 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:15.982
After his acquittal

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.017
in the Senate impeachment trial
yesterday,

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.418
Trump was eager to celebrate --

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.821
even at events where
it wasn't entirely appropriate.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.189
For example, this morning,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.692
he attended the annual
National Prayer Breakfast

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.994
in Washington,
and before he even sat down,

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:30.129
Trump started holding up
the front pages

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:33.532
of multiple newspapers
showing people he was acquitted,

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.702
a stunt which he then repeated
at a press conference

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:38.170
a few hours later
at the White House.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.274
He finally found the one job
he's qualified for --

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.642
newspaper boy.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.945
[ As Trump ] Extra! Extra!

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.682
Extra! Extra! Read all about me!

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.185
Trump "a-quitter."

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.953
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.487
[ Normal voice ]
Then Trump took aim at both

00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:56.756
Utah senator Mitt Romney,

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.858
the only Republican
who voted to convict Trump,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.694
and also House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.029
Romney cited his faith
in explaining his vote,

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:05.431
and Pelosi had said
many times

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:06.766
that she prays
for the president.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.135
and Trump decided
to attack them for it.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:13.639
-I don't like people who use
their faith

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:17.209
as justification for doing

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:20.546
what they know is wrong.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:25.684
Nor do I like people who say,
"I pray for you."

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:28.988
When they know that
that's not so.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.523
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:36.062
-Because what is prayer, if not
a time to air petty grievances?

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.430
Then Trump's son Don Jr.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.298
tried to back him up on Twitter
this morning, writing,

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.500
"The likelihood of Nancy Pelosi
praying for Trump

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.569
is about the same
as the likelihood of Satan

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:45.672
running around
quoting the scriptures."

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.039
All right. Okay.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.874
Let's see if Satan has ever
quoted the scriptures.

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.176
-2 Corinthians, right?

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.412
2 Corinthians 3:17.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.347
That's the whole ball game.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.149
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.149 --> 00:02:00.153
-Even when Trump is reading
directly from the Bible,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.520
he sounds like
he's making it up.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.123
He sounds like he's trying
to distract a priest

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.558
while his fellow altar boys
steal the communion wine.

00:02:06.558 --> 00:02:07.794
[ As Trump ]
2 Corinthians, oh.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.461
There were --
Wasn't just one Corinthian.

00:02:09.461 --> 00:02:11.096
There were two.

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.865
That's what -- That's what
really made 'em quite a team.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.700
And, you know, you just can't
beat 2 Corinthians.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.737
I mean, that's the whole
ball game.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.405
[ Normal voice ] Then Trump
moved over to the White House,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.208
where he decided to hold
his deranged victory speech

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.477
or press conference
or whatever it was.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.745
In fact, even Trump himself

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.314
didn't seem to know
what quite to call it.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.349
-This is really not
a news conference.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.118
It's not a speech.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.585
It's not anything.

00:02:33.585 --> 00:02:36.822
-Then why are we here?

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.425
He sounds like Simon Cowell
berating a contestant

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.860
on "America's Got Talent."

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.228
[ As Cowell ] It's not a song.
It's not a dance.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.496
It's not anything.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.966
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.204
[ Normal voice ]
That might be

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.705
the only thing Trump
was right about.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:55.074
This really wasn't a speech or
a press conference or anything.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.742
It was a chance to lash out
at critics,

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:59.778
spin wild conspiracy theories,
and sooth his wounded ego.

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:01.113
In fact, he spent most
of his time

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.216
gleefully shouting out
to fellow Republicans

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.783
who helped him cover up
his crimes.

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.453
And the shout-outs kept
getting weirder and weirder.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.954
-Mitch McConnell,
I want to tell you,

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:12.658
you did a fantastic job.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.127
And Mike Braun,
you have done some great job.

00:03:15.127 --> 00:03:16.195
Thank you very much.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.563
Josh Hawley,
I want to thank you.

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.799
You were right
from the beginning.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.901
Man, did I make a good choice.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:25.838
But Mike Lee is a brilliant guy.
He's difficult.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.240
Kevin, man, did you do a job.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.242
Lucky you're there.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.443
Jim Jordan.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:34.580
When I first got to know Jim,
I said, uh,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.017
"Huh, never wears a jacket.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.652
The hell's going on?

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.821
He's obviously
very proud of his body."

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.857
-Proud of his body? Have you --
Have you seen Jim Jordan?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.292
He looks like
a ventriloquist dummy

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.194
who got cut
from Jeff Dunham's act.

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:52.231
Also, it is so telling,
so telling that Trump

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.367
thinks not wearing a jacket
means you're proud of your body

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.869
because Trump does everything
he can to cover up his body.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.973
Not only does he wear those
baggy pants and long ties,

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.241
but he also wears
that giant bulky coat

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:05.043
that makes him look like he just
snuck out of the White House

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:08.647
with all the valuable china
stuffed in his pockets.

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:10.049
Then, at one point,
Trump shouted out

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.685
Iowa senator Chuck Grassley
and claimed Grassley

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:16.121
had supposedly scared
former FBI Director James Comey

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:18.791
into confessing to Comey's
supposed secret plot

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.926
to take down Trump.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:25.063
-A man who got James Comey
to choke.

00:04:25.063 --> 00:04:27.366
And he was just talking
in his regular voice.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:31.170
He's got this voice
that scares people.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.540
You know, people from Iowa
can be very tough.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.776
We're doing very well in Iowa,
but I'll tell you,

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.145
Chuck Grassley,
he's looking at Comey...

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:42.081
[ Deep voice ] "Well,
you tell me. What did you say?"

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.783
-All right, that sounds
very scary,

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.686
so let's compare this scary
fictional version of Grassley

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.921
to the actual Grassley
trying to gavel down

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.823
a Democrat at a Senate hearing.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.158
-This committee, sir...
[ Gavel banging ]

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.393
...is in violation
of even the values

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:56.195
I've heard you talk about
time and time again,

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.931
the ideals that we should have.
What is the rush?

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.432
[ Banging continues ]
What are we trying to hide

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:02.735
by not having
the documents out front?

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.637
What is with the rush?
What are we hiding

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.039
by not letting
those documents come out?

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.509
You've called for documents --
you, yourself.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.744
Let me at the documents.
We thought there should be more.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.546
We have not received
the documents

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.247
that you have even called for.

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:18.584
-He's not a senator.
He's a metronome.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:21.287
Looks like a grandpa who's been
trying to hammer one nail

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.722
into the deck for eight hours.

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.690
"Grandpa, just let me
use the drill."

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.293
[ Gruff voice ]
I don't need any help!

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.228
Let me do it myself!

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.063
[ Normal voice ] Although,
there was one imaginary friend

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.332
Trump couldn't introduce
because he wasn't in the room,

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.668
but Trump said he wished
he had been there

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.136
so that he could have given him
an introduction, too.

00:05:38.136 --> 00:05:39.472
-"Honest Abe" Lincoln.

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.874
A lot of people
forget Abe Lincoln.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.477
I wish he were here. I'd give
him one hell of an introduction.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.445
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.214
But he was a Republican.

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:50.983
Abe Lincoln, Honest Abe.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.551
-That's right.
Trump wishes he could have

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.720
introduced Abraham Lincoln
in his speech today.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.055
Of course, if Trump did,

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.523
he would immediately make it
about him

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.858
and somehow insult Lincoln.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.960
[ As Trump ] Honest Abe.
There he is.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.395
Abe Lincoln, everybody.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.197
So honest,
maybe the most honest,

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.832
although some people say
I'm a little more honest.

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.402
So Abe over there,
he's laughing.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:11.670
He's number two,
the second-most honest.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:12.839
I'm number one.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:15.074
I told you not to go
to that theater, Abe!

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:16.642
I told you.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.345
I told you plays were boring,
but of course, you're fine.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.513
Nothing happened to you,

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:22.114
so I don't know
why the audience groaned.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.116
You're here in this timeline.

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.451
In this timeline, you're fine.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.286
You're 200 years old
and you're right there

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:31.156
and you're laughing at me
and we're friends.

00:06:31.156 --> 00:06:33.025
[ Normal voice ] Trump's
rambling non-speech fever dream

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:35.261
or whatever the hell it was
was really just a showcase

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.796
for our perpetually aggrieved

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.731
and wounded president
to nurse his ego,

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:41.500
relive old glories,
and lash out at random critics

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.001
and shout away
imagined opponents.

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:45.004
For example, Trump claimed
that his three years

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.539
as president have been marred

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.340
by traitors
trying to take him down

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.277
and kept using a few
insane phrases in particular.

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.779
-It was evil. It was corrupt.

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:56.515
It was dirty cops.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.483
It was leakers and liars.

00:06:58.483 --> 00:07:01.854
The bad ones, the leakers,
the liars, the dirty cops.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:04.056
Horrible dirty cops.

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:07.526
When I fired that sleaze bag,
he was the top scum.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:10.229
We caught him in the act.

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:12.231
Dirty cops.

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:15.534
-Is he whining about impeachment
or narrating a movie trailer?

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:16.635
[ As Trump ]
It was the bad ones,

00:07:16.635 --> 00:07:19.071
the leakers,
the liars, the dirty cops.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:22.275
And the only one who could
take them down was Serpi-Dope.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:24.076
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:25.311
[ Normal voice ]
I hope this is a reminder

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:26.712
to everyone who thought Trump

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:28.347
has somehow managed
to restrain himself

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:30.149
during the State of the Union
two days ago.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.718
The Trump we saw today
was the real Trump,

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:34.253
and it's the Trump
we're gonna keep seeing

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.888
for the next nine months
until the election,

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:38.925
because it's pretty clear from
his vengeful celebratory tone

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:41.394
that Trump wanted this to be
the week that for all intents

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:44.696
and purposes, he kicked off
his 2020 re-election campaign.

00:07:44.696 --> 00:07:47.900
Although I'm not sure Trump
ever really stopped campaigning.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.303
He spends more time in arenas
than Jon Bon Jovi.

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:53.372
[ As Trump ]
You ready to rock, Kansas?

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:55.641
[ Normal voice ]
"This is Missouri, you idiot!"

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.275
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:57.275 --> 00:08:01.847
For example, during his
White House tirade today,

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:04.016
Trump bragged about his
near-unanimous victory

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.918
in the Republican Iowa
caucus on Monday,

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:08.087
even though he's
the incumbent president

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.755
and everyone expected him
to win easily.

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.457
But Trump still sent a big team

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:13.391
to Iowa on Monday
as a show of force,

00:08:13.391 --> 00:08:16.829
including his adult
gargoyle sons, Eric and Don Jr.

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:20.232
And Don Jr. relayed what Iowans
have been telling him

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:22.200
throughout his time
campaigning in the state.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.803
-Honestly, the biggest thing
I get is thanks.

00:08:24.803 --> 00:08:26.805
It's someone telling us
thank you

00:08:26.805 --> 00:08:28.741
for the sacrifices
that your family is making,

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:31.343
because you didn't need
this job, right?

00:08:31.343 --> 00:08:34.146
The presidency wasn't the next
natural progression

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:35.915
for my father like it
would have been for Hillary

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:38.517
where it's her turn.
Right?

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:39.819
He'd actually done things
in the real world.

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.687
He needed this job, frankly,
like a hole in the head,

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:43.421
especially understanding
the resistance

00:08:43.421 --> 00:08:44.923
that he was gonna get.

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:48.827
-Ah, but are you sure he doesn't
already have a hole in his head?

00:08:48.827 --> 00:08:50.195
Listen to him talk and tell me

00:08:50.195 --> 00:08:53.465
he doesn't have
some hole in his head.

00:08:53.465 --> 00:08:57.269
-10,000 known or suspested
gang members.

00:08:57.269 --> 00:08:59.337
Advising lawmarkers.

00:08:59.337 --> 00:09:03.409
Will not be tolerited.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.277
-Yes, you see,
Democratic lawmarkers

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:07.512
suspested that Trump
had committed a crime,

00:09:07.512 --> 00:09:11.483
but ultimately Republicans
decided it could be tolerited.

00:09:11.483 --> 00:09:12.852
That was Monday,
and then on Wednesday,

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:15.320
Trump was hoping his week
would be propelled even further

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.456
by an acquittal
in the Senate on party lines,

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:20.226
where he expected to receive
100% support from Republicans.

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:22.527
And while it's true
that Trump was acquitted,

00:09:22.527 --> 00:09:24.263
his good news was stepped on
by the fact

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:25.898
that Republican senator
Mitt Romney

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.866
sided with Democrats
and voted to convict him.

00:09:27.866 --> 00:09:31.237
Romney rained on Trump's parade,
which is bad news for Trump,

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:34.373
because he doesn't know
how to use an umbrella.

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:37.443
But seriously,
even with the acquittal,

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.345
that one vote
is a historical stain

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:41.279
that will remain
on Trump's presidency forever.

00:09:41.279 --> 00:09:42.547
That fact's gonna show up

00:09:42.547 --> 00:09:44.617
on Trivial Pursuit
cards years from now.

00:09:44.617 --> 00:09:46.385
"Who is the only president
in history

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.186
to have a senator
of his own party

00:09:48.186 --> 00:09:49.922
vote to remove him from office?

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.389
Hint -- The answer is not..."

00:09:51.389 --> 00:09:53.959
-Abe Lincoln, Honest Abe.

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:55.394
-Now, Romney knew he would pay

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:56.762
a political price
for this decision

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.497
because Trump allies had already
warned

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:00.232
that if Republicans
vote against the president,

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:01.533
your head will be on a pike.

00:10:01.533 --> 00:10:03.669
And Romney was asked
about that danger

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.403
in an interview on Fox News.

00:10:05.403 --> 00:10:08.774
-You realize this is war.

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:13.646
Donald Trump will never
forgive you for this.

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:15.548
-There's a hymn that is sung
in my church.

00:10:15.548 --> 00:10:17.816
It's an old protestant hymn
which is

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:19.751
"Do what is right,
let the consequence follow."

00:10:19.751 --> 00:10:21.854
-There's probably no better way
to flummox Donald Trump

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:23.322
than by quoting a religious hymn

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:24.957
because he has no idea
what it means.

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:27.927
When Trump hears the phrase,
"old protestant hymn,"

00:10:27.927 --> 00:10:29.095
he probably thinks
he's referring

00:10:29.095 --> 00:10:30.495
to a member of his cabinet.

00:10:30.495 --> 00:10:32.664
[ As Trump ] Oh, yeah, I got
a bunch of old protestant "hims"

00:10:32.664 --> 00:10:35.867
and I got one protestant "her."

00:10:35.867 --> 00:10:37.303
[ Normal voice ]
And sure enough,

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:40.806
Trump did fire back at Romney
yesterday with a bizarre ad

00:10:40.806 --> 00:10:42.575
aimed at a member
of his own party

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:45.510
accusing Romney of being
a secret Democratic traitor.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.380
But I'm not sure the ad had
quite the damaging effect

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.616
on Romney
that Trump hoped it would have.

00:10:50.616 --> 00:10:52.884
-Slick, slippery, stealthy.

00:10:52.884 --> 00:10:54.719
Mitt Romney had us fooled.

00:10:54.719 --> 00:10:57.189
Posing as a Republican,
he tried to infiltrate

00:10:57.189 --> 00:10:59.791
Trump's administration
as Secretary of State.

00:10:59.791 --> 00:11:01.493
Now his cover's blown,

00:11:01.493 --> 00:11:05.497
exposed by news reports
as a Democrat secret asset.

00:11:05.497 --> 00:11:08.633
-Look, I'm no Mitt Romney
superfan,

00:11:08.633 --> 00:11:13.439
but you do realize this ad makes
him look incredibly cool, right?

00:11:13.439 --> 00:11:14.706
I mean, I didn't think
it was possible

00:11:14.706 --> 00:11:17.475
to take a boring private
equity robot like Romney

00:11:17.475 --> 00:11:20.646
and turn him into James Bond,
but somehow Trump did it.

00:11:20.646 --> 00:11:22.614
Literally wearing sunglasses,

00:11:22.614 --> 00:11:26.184
and you describe him as slick,
stealthy, and a secret asset.

00:11:26.184 --> 00:11:28.520
You might as well give him
a martini and Aston Martin

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.222
and put him next
to Pussy Galore.

00:11:31.222 --> 00:11:33.492
[ As Romney ] Uh, Ms. Galore,
do you mind if I read you

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:36.061
an old protestant hymn?

00:11:36.061 --> 00:11:37.229
[ As Galore ]
Call me Pussy, Mitt.

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:38.563
[ As Romney ]
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:11:38.563 --> 00:11:41.466
No, no, no,
I'm not gonna do that.

00:11:41.466 --> 00:11:43.435
Definitely not.

00:11:43.435 --> 00:11:44.870
[ Normal voice ] And yet,
while Romney stood alone

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.072
among Republicans
in holding Trump accountable,

00:11:47.072 --> 00:11:50.109
others who voted to acquit Trump
tried to dodge questions

00:11:50.109 --> 00:11:52.711
about their votes, especially
the deeply vulnerable senators

00:11:52.711 --> 00:11:55.347
facing re-election
in swing states in 2020.

00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:56.982
Take Maine senator
Susan Collins,

00:11:56.982 --> 00:11:58.484
who sided with Trump
on impeachment,

00:11:58.484 --> 00:12:00.685
but also tried to claim
in an interview with Fox News

00:12:00.685 --> 00:12:02.621
last night that Trump
had learned his lesson.

00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:05.024
-Will something in you
be disappointed

00:12:05.024 --> 00:12:08.761
if you never see any evidence
that he has learned a lesson

00:12:08.761 --> 00:12:10.862
or if he does something
like this again?

00:12:10.862 --> 00:12:12.497
-Very much so.

00:12:12.497 --> 00:12:15.768
I hoped that the president
would have learned

00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:19.371
from the fact that
he was impeached by the House.

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:23.241
There were so many of us who
are Republicans in the Senate

00:12:23.241 --> 00:12:25.410
who are very critical
of the call.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.112
The call was wrong.

00:12:27.112 --> 00:12:28.980
Parts of the call were fine.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:31.550
-What do you mean,
parts of the call were fine?

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:32.918
"He nailed the 'Hello,'

00:12:32.918 --> 00:12:36.254
and I thought the 'Goodbye'
was solid, too.

00:12:36.254 --> 00:12:39.091
Put it back in the cradle
when he was done."

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:40.592
Also, why do you think Trump
would have learned anything?

00:12:40.592 --> 00:12:42.394
Just today, he said
the call was perfect again.

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:43.996
Trump is incapable of learning.

00:12:43.996 --> 00:12:45.197
Doesn't matter what the subject
is --

00:12:45.197 --> 00:12:46.732
spelling, geography,
he never learns.

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:48.333
Remember, this is a guy
who misspelled

00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:49.901
his wife's name
and his own name

00:12:49.901 --> 00:12:54.640
and who has literally invented
multiple fake countries.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.876
-Tanzania. Nambia.

00:12:56.876 --> 00:12:59.845
-Yes -- Tanzania and Nambia.

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:01.013
This guy is the president,

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:02.914
and he doesn't even know
basic geography.

00:13:02.914 --> 00:13:05.317
If you said "Bangladesh"
to Trump, he'd go...

00:13:05.317 --> 00:13:07.519
[ As Trump ]
Why? Is Ladesh hot?

00:13:07.519 --> 00:13:12.158
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:13:16.662 --> 00:13:18.864
[ Normal voice ] Collins
was then asked if Trump

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:20.599
had given her any assurances

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:23.035
that he had learned his lesson,
and she admitted he had not.

00:13:23.035 --> 00:13:25.904
-Did he give you any assurance
that he would not

00:13:25.904 --> 00:13:28.373
do something like that again,
accept foreign help

00:13:28.373 --> 00:13:30.676
in anything related to someone
that might be running with him?

00:13:30.676 --> 00:13:32.177
Did you talk to him
about it at all?

00:13:32.177 --> 00:13:35.781
-I've had no conversations
with him throughout the trial.

00:13:35.781 --> 00:13:38.216
-So, why do you have that
feeling that he has changed,

00:13:38.216 --> 00:13:39.218
that he learned a lesson?

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:41.253
-Well, I may not
be correct on that.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:44.056
It's more aspirational
on my part.

00:13:44.056 --> 00:13:45.724
-Oh, it's aspirational.
That's nice.

00:13:45.724 --> 00:13:47.760
Do you have one of those
motivational posters

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.094
up in your office, you know,

00:13:49.094 --> 00:13:50.429
like the one with the cat
that says,

00:13:50.429 --> 00:13:53.264
"Hang in there.
He might not be a criminal."

00:13:53.264 --> 00:13:55.200
Then there was Colorado senator
Cory Gardner,

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.768
another deeply vulnerable
Republican

00:13:56.768 --> 00:13:58.803
facing a tough re-election
in a swing state.

00:13:58.803 --> 00:14:00.606
Gardner also sided with Trump
on impeachment.

00:14:00.606 --> 00:14:02.474
Last night,
on a local news station,

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:05.143
he was asked repeatedly if
Trump's actions were appropriate

00:14:05.143 --> 00:14:06.445
and would not answer
the question,

00:14:06.445 --> 00:14:09.448
while also insisting
he was answering the question.

00:14:09.448 --> 00:14:10.849
-Do you believe it's appropriate

00:14:10.849 --> 00:14:12.784
for the president
of the United States

00:14:12.784 --> 00:14:16.021
to ask a foreign leader to
investigate a political rival?

00:14:16.021 --> 00:14:17.456
Yes or no?
-That wasn't the question

00:14:17.456 --> 00:14:19.357
that we had last night,
or that we had in impeachment.

00:14:19.357 --> 00:14:21.526
-Was the president's behavior
appropriate, though?

00:14:21.526 --> 00:14:22.695
-But that wasn't the question.

00:14:22.695 --> 00:14:25.430
-So, clearly, not answering
that question.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:27.933
-Well, I did answer the question
about impeachment.

00:14:27.933 --> 00:14:30.202
-No, you didn't.
These guys all have

00:14:30.202 --> 00:14:32.337
the same Trump brain disease
where they think they can

00:14:32.337 --> 00:14:35.273
just Jedi mind trick us into not
believing what we're seeing.

00:14:35.273 --> 00:14:36.641
That's why Trump's always
doing that thing

00:14:36.641 --> 00:14:37.943
with his hands, you know?

00:14:37.943 --> 00:14:40.379
He's trying to pull
an Obi Wan Kenobi on us,

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:42.381
but instead, he just
looks like he's playing

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:43.715
an invisible accordion.

00:14:43.715 --> 00:14:45.117
[ As Trump ] Those aren't
the droids you're looking for.

00:14:45.117 --> 00:14:47.652
You guys want to hear a polka?

00:14:47.652 --> 00:14:50.255
You want to hear a polka?

00:14:50.255 --> 00:14:53.859
[ Normal voice ] The fundamental
tenets of Trumpism

00:14:53.859 --> 00:14:56.395
and the modern Republican party
are grievance and paranoia,

00:14:56.395 --> 00:14:57.729
and that was on full display

00:14:57.729 --> 00:14:59.531
in Trump's deranged
press conference today.

00:14:59.531 --> 00:15:01.500
But vulnerable Republicans
in swing states

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.068
are struggling
to defend that behavior

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:05.304
because a majority
of Americans in polls

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:08.073
still believe that the
president's crimes cannot be...

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:10.776
-Tolerited.
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:10.776 --> 00:15:12.444
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:14.380 line:0%
♪♪

